IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g5-interpretation`
IMPORT `g5-nouns`
IMPORT `g5-art14-court-powers`

-- g5-tests-art14.l4: tests of Article 14 (powers of the court over a registered charity).  Every expected value was decided from the Law's text
-- (quoted above each group) before the run.  A DEONTIC has no equality, so each regulative rule is run with #TRACE and the expectation sits in an
-- EXPECT comment right above the trace (checked by check-traces.py): FULFILLED, BREACH or STANDING (the rule is printed back, still open).

§ `Tests of Article 14 (powers of court over registered charity)`

§§ `Cases used below`

`the favoured reading` MEANS `the favoured interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`

-- Fields: the conduct concerns the administration of the charity; it is misconduct in the ordinary sense; it is necessary or desirable to exercise the power to protect the property.
`misconduct in the administration of the charity` MEANS `What appears to the court under Article 14(1)` WITH
    `the conduct concerns the administration of the charity` IS TRUE
    `the conduct is misconduct in the ordinary sense` IS TRUE
    `it is necessary or desirable to exercise the power to protect the charity's property or secure its proper application` IS FALSE

-- A governor's conviction for a tax offence committed "in relation to" the charity (Article 2(10)(b)(iii)), so misconduct within Article 2(10), but with no bearing on the administration of the charity.
`a governor's conviction with no bearing on the administration` MEANS `What appears to the court under Article 14(1)` WITH
    `the conduct concerns the administration of the charity` IS FALSE
    `the conduct is misconduct in the ordinary sense` IS FALSE
    `it is necessary or desirable to exercise the power to protect the charity's property or secure its proper application` IS FALSE

-- Mismanagement in the administration that is not a contravention of any provision, so not misconduct within Article 2(10).
`mismanagement that is not defined misconduct` MEANS `What appears to the court under Article 14(1)` WITH
    `the conduct concerns the administration of the charity` IS TRUE
    `the conduct is misconduct in the ordinary sense` IS TRUE
    `it is necessary or desirable to exercise the power to protect the charity's property or secure its proper application` IS FALSE

`only protection of the property is needed` MEANS `What appears to the court under Article 14(1)` WITH
    `the conduct concerns the administration of the charity` IS FALSE
    `the conduct is misconduct in the ordinary sense` IS FALSE
    `it is necessary or desirable to exercise the power to protect the charity's property or secure its proper application` IS TRUE

`nothing appears to the court` MEANS `What appears to the court under Article 14(1)` WITH
    `the conduct concerns the administration of the charity` IS FALSE
    `the conduct is misconduct in the ordinary sense` IS FALSE
    `it is necessary or desirable to exercise the power to protect the charity's property or secure its proper application` IS FALSE

§§ `Article 14(1): when the powers are exercisable`

-- src:407 | (1) The court may exercise any of the powers set out in paragraph (2) in relation to a registered charity if, on an application by the Commissioner or the Attorney General, it appears to the court –
-- src:408 | (a) that there is or has been misconduct in the administration of the charity; or
-- src:409 | (b) that it is necessary or desirable to exercise the power for the purpose of protecting the property of the charity or securing a proper application of that property in accordance with the charity's registered charitable purposes and registered public benefit statement.
-- Arguments: the interpretation; the entity is a registered charity; who applied; the conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10); what appears.

-- The applicants.
#ASSERT `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` `the favoured reading` TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` TRUE `misconduct in the administration of the charity`
#ASSERT `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` `the favoured reading` TRUE `an application by the Attorney General` TRUE `misconduct in the administration of the charity`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` `the favoured reading` TRUE `an application by the registered charity` TRUE `misconduct in the administration of the charity`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` `the favoured reading` TRUE `an application by a person to whom the order was directed` TRUE `misconduct in the administration of the charity`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` `the favoured reading` TRUE `an application by any other person` TRUE `misconduct in the administration of the charity`
-- "in relation to a registered charity".
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` `the favoured reading` FALSE `an application by the Commissioner` TRUE `misconduct in the administration of the charity`
-- The two grounds are alternatives ("or"): (b) alone suffices, and neither ground is no ground.
#ASSERT `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` `the favoured reading` TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` FALSE `only protection of the property is needed`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` `the favoured reading` TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` FALSE `nothing appears to the court`
-- Fork F5.4.  A governor's conviction that bears on no administration: misconduct within Article 2(10), but not "in the administration of the charity".
-- Reading A (taken): not enough.  Reading B: enough.  Reading C (ordinary sense): not enough.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` `the favoured reading` TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` TRUE `a governor's conviction with no bearing on the administration`
#ASSERT `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` `the interpretation with any misconduct` TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` TRUE `a governor's conviction with no bearing on the administration`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` `the interpretation with misconduct in the ordinary sense` TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` TRUE `a governor's conviction with no bearing on the administration`
-- Mismanagement in the administration that is not misconduct within Article 2(10): A and B refuse it, C accepts it.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` `the favoured reading` TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` FALSE `mismanagement that is not defined misconduct`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` `the interpretation with any misconduct` TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` FALSE `mismanagement that is not defined misconduct`
#ASSERT `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` `the interpretation with misconduct in the ordinary sense` TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` FALSE `mismanagement that is not defined misconduct`
-- Defined misconduct in the administration satisfies all three readings.
#ASSERT `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` `the interpretation with any misconduct` TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` TRUE `misconduct in the administration of the charity`
#ASSERT `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` `the interpretation with misconduct in the ordinary sense` TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` TRUE `misconduct in the administration of the charity`
-- The three readings called directly.
#ASSERT `F5.4 A: misconduct within Article 2(10) that bears on the administration of the charity` TRUE `misconduct in the administration of the charity`
#ASSERT NOT `F5.4 A: misconduct within Article 2(10) that bears on the administration of the charity` TRUE `a governor's conviction with no bearing on the administration`
#ASSERT `F5.4 B: any misconduct within Article 2(10)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `F5.4 B: any misconduct within Article 2(10)` FALSE
#ASSERT `F5.4 C: misconduct in the ordinary sense in the administration of the charity` `mismanagement that is not defined misconduct`
#ASSERT NOT `F5.4 C: misconduct in the ordinary sense in the administration of the charity` `a governor's conviction with no bearing on the administration`

-- The application and the court's permission, as a regulative rule.  The Commissioner applies as whoever is acting as the Commissioner.
-- Arguments: the interpretation; registered charity; someone is acting as the Commissioner; who applied; misconduct within Article 2(10); what appears.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 14(1) the court may exercise the powers on the application` `the favoured reading` TRUE TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` TRUE `misconduct in the administration of the charity` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `apply to the court` `an application by the Commissioner` AT 3
    PARTY `the court` DOES `exercise the powers set out in Article 14(2)` AT 9

-- The Attorney General applies; the court acts.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 14(1) the court may exercise the powers on the application` `the favoured reading` TRUE FALSE `an application by the Attorney General` TRUE `misconduct in the administration of the charity` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Attorney General` DOES `apply to the court` `an application by the Attorney General` AT 3
    PARTY `the court` DOES `exercise the powers set out in Article 14(2)` AT 9

-- The application is made but the court has not acted: its permission is still open (and unused it is no breach).
-- EXPECT: STANDING MAY
#TRACE `Art 14(1) the court may exercise the powers on the application` `the favoured reading` TRUE TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` TRUE `misconduct in the administration of the charity` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `apply to the court` `an application by the Commissioner` AT 3

-- No application yet: the Commissioner's permission to apply stands.
-- EXPECT: STANDING MAY
#TRACE `Art 14(1) the court may exercise the powers on the application` `the favoured reading` TRUE TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` TRUE `misconduct in the administration of the charity` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- The grounds do not appear to the court: the application is made and the court has nothing to exercise.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 14(1) the court may exercise the powers on the application` `the favoured reading` TRUE TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` FALSE `nothing appears to the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `apply to the court` `an application by the Commissioner` AT 3

-- Nobody is acting as the Commissioner: no application by the Commissioner.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 14(1) the court may exercise the powers on the application` `the favoured reading` TRUE FALSE `an application by the Commissioner` TRUE `misconduct in the administration of the charity` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- An application by the registered charity, or by anyone else, opens no power under Article 14(1).
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 14(1) the court may exercise the powers on the application` `the favoured reading` TRUE TRUE `an application by the registered charity` TRUE `misconduct in the administration of the charity` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 14(1) the court may exercise the powers on the application` `the favoured reading` TRUE TRUE `an application by any other person` TRUE `misconduct in the administration of the charity` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 14(1) the court may exercise the powers on the application` `the favoured reading` FALSE TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` TRUE `misconduct in the administration of the charity` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

§§ `Article 14(2): any order the court sees fit`

-- src:410 | (2) The court may make any order that the court sees fit to remedy the misconduct, protect the property and secure its proper application.
@ref Article 14(2) (src:410)
`an order to remedy the misconduct only` MEANS `Order that the court sees fit under Article 14(2)` WITH `to remedy the misconduct` IS TRUE, `to protect the property` IS FALSE, `to secure its proper application` IS FALSE
`an order to protect the property only` MEANS `Order that the court sees fit under Article 14(2)` WITH `to remedy the misconduct` IS FALSE, `to protect the property` IS TRUE, `to secure its proper application` IS FALSE
`an order to secure the proper application only` MEANS `Order that the court sees fit under Article 14(2)` WITH `to remedy the misconduct` IS FALSE, `to protect the property` IS FALSE, `to secure its proper application` IS TRUE
`an order serving all three purposes` MEANS `Order that the court sees fit under Article 14(2)` WITH `to remedy the misconduct` IS TRUE, `to protect the property` IS TRUE, `to secure its proper application` IS TRUE
`an order serving none of the purposes` MEANS `Order that the court sees fit under Article 14(2)` WITH `to remedy the misconduct` IS FALSE, `to protect the property` IS FALSE, `to secure its proper application` IS FALSE

-- Fork F5.12.  Reading A (taken): at least one of the three purposes.
#ASSERT `Art 14(2) the order is one the court sees fit` `the favoured reading` `an order to remedy the misconduct only`
#ASSERT `Art 14(2) the order is one the court sees fit` `the favoured reading` `an order to protect the property only`
#ASSERT `Art 14(2) the order is one the court sees fit` `the favoured reading` `an order to secure the proper application only`
#ASSERT `Art 14(2) the order is one the court sees fit` `the favoured reading` `an order serving all three purposes`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(2) the order is one the court sees fit` `the favoured reading` `an order serving none of the purposes`
-- Reading B: all three; an order that only protects the property is then not available.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(2) the order is one the court sees fit` `the interpretation with all three purposes` `an order to protect the property only`
#ASSERT `Art 14(2) the order is one the court sees fit` `the interpretation with all three purposes` `an order serving all three purposes`
-- The case that discriminates: ground (b) alone (nothing to remedy), and an order that protects the property.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 14(2) the court may make any order it sees fit` `the favoured reading` TRUE `an application by the Attorney General` FALSE `only protection of the property is needed` `an order to protect the property only` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `make an order that the court sees fit` AT 12

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 14(2) the court may make any order it sees fit` `the interpretation with all three purposes` TRUE `an application by the Attorney General` FALSE `only protection of the property is needed` `an order to protect the property only` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- Where the powers are exercisable and the order serves a purpose: the permission is open; unused, it is no breach.
-- EXPECT: STANDING MAY
#TRACE `Art 14(2) the court may make any order it sees fit` `the favoured reading` TRUE `an application by the Attorney General` FALSE `only protection of the property is needed` `an order to protect the property only` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- Powers not exercisable (an application by a stranger): no permission.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 14(2) the court may make any order it sees fit` `the favoured reading` TRUE `an application by any other person` TRUE `misconduct in the administration of the charity` `an order to remedy the misconduct only` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

§§ `Article 14(3): the nine kinds of order`

-- src:411 | (3) Without prejudice to the generality of paragraph (2), the orders that the court may make include an order –
-- src:412 | (a) prohibiting (whether for a specified or indefinite period) the charity or a governor from –
-- src:413 | (i) referring to or holding out the entity as a charity or Jersey charity, or as being charitable, having charitable purposes or providing public benefit,
-- src:414 | (ii) soliciting donations from the public, as specified in the order, or
-- src:415 | (iii) taking any other action specified in the order;
-- src:416 | (b) appointing a person (whether a specified or indefinite period) to manage the affairs of the charity in place of its governors;
-- src:417 | (c) appointing a person to be a governor of the charity;
-- src:418 | (d) suspending or removing a governor of the charity, or any other person concerned in the management or control of the charity;
-- src:419 | (e) requiring a person (including without prejudice a person carrying on regulated financial services business) who holds property on behalf of the charity, or on behalf of a governor of the charity, not to part with the property without the court’s consent;
-- src:420 | (f) restricting the transactions that may be entered into, or the nature or amount of the payments that may be made, in the administration of the charity without the court’s consent;
-- src:421 | (g) making the administration of the charity subject to such supervision, restraint or conditions, from such time, and for such periods, as the court may specify;
-- src:422 | (h) requiring a governor who appears to the court to have engaged in any misconduct, or any other person who appears to be responsible for any misconduct, to take such steps as the court may direct to remedy the effects of the misconduct;
-- src:423 | (i) making such ancillary provision as the court thinks desirable.
@ref Article 14(3) (src:411-423)
-- Fields: kind; directed at; what a prohibition forbids; it appears to the court that the person engaged in misconduct or is responsible for it; period.
`the period of a hold on payments, from 1 June 2026 for 30 days` MEANS `a specified period` (YMD 2026 6 1) 30
`an indefinite period from 1 June 2026` MEANS `an indefinite period` (YMD 2026 6 1)

`a prohibition on holding out as a charity, directed at the charity` MEANS `Order proposed under Article 14(3)` WITH
    kind IS `an order prohibiting the charity or a governor from holding out as a charity, soliciting donations or another specified action`
    `directed at` IS `the charity`
    forbids IS JUST `referring to or holding out the entity as a charity or Jersey charity, or as being charitable, having charitable purposes or providing public benefit`
    `it appears to the court that the person at whom the order is directed has engaged in misconduct or is responsible for it` IS FALSE
    period IS `an indefinite period from 1 June 2026`

`a prohibition on soliciting donations, directed at a governor` MEANS `Order proposed under Article 14(3)` WITH
    kind IS `an order prohibiting the charity or a governor from holding out as a charity, soliciting donations or another specified action`
    `directed at` IS `a governor of the charity`
    forbids IS JUST `soliciting donations from the public, as specified in the order`
    `it appears to the court that the person at whom the order is directed has engaged in misconduct or is responsible for it` IS FALSE
    period IS `the period of a hold on payments, from 1 June 2026 for 30 days`

`a prohibition that says nothing of what it forbids` MEANS `Order proposed under Article 14(3)` WITH
    kind IS `an order prohibiting the charity or a governor from holding out as a charity, soliciting donations or another specified action`
    `directed at` IS `the charity`
    forbids IS NOTHING
    `it appears to the court that the person at whom the order is directed has engaged in misconduct or is responsible for it` IS FALSE
    period IS `an indefinite period from 1 June 2026`

`a prohibition directed at a person holding property for the charity` MEANS `Order proposed under Article 14(3)` WITH
    kind IS `an order prohibiting the charity or a governor from holding out as a charity, soliciting donations or another specified action`
    `directed at` IS `a person who holds property on behalf of the charity`
    forbids IS JUST `taking any other action specified in the order`
    `it appears to the court that the person at whom the order is directed has engaged in misconduct or is responsible for it` IS FALSE
    period IS `an indefinite period from 1 June 2026`

`an order appointing a manager` MEANS `Order proposed under Article 14(3)` WITH
    kind IS `an order appointing a person to manage the affairs of the charity in place of its governors`
    `directed at` IS `no person in particular`
    forbids IS NOTHING
    `it appears to the court that the person at whom the order is directed has engaged in misconduct or is responsible for it` IS FALSE
    period IS `an indefinite period from 1 June 2026`

`an order appointing a governor` MEANS `Order proposed under Article 14(3)` WITH
    kind IS `an order appointing a person to be a governor`
    `directed at` IS `no person in particular`
    forbids IS NOTHING
    `it appears to the court that the person at whom the order is directed has engaged in misconduct or is responsible for it` IS FALSE
    period IS `an indefinite period from 1 June 2026`

`an order suspending a governor` MEANS `Order proposed under Article 14(3)` WITH
    kind IS `an order suspending or removing a governor or another person concerned in the management`
    `directed at` IS `a governor of the charity`
    forbids IS NOTHING
    `it appears to the court that the person at whom the order is directed has engaged in misconduct or is responsible for it` IS FALSE
    period IS `an indefinite period from 1 June 2026`

`an order removing the finance manager` MEANS `Order proposed under Article 14(3)` WITH
    kind IS `an order suspending or removing a governor or another person concerned in the management`
    `directed at` IS `another person concerned in the management or control of the charity`
    forbids IS NOTHING
    `it appears to the court that the person at whom the order is directed has engaged in misconduct or is responsible for it` IS FALSE
    period IS `an indefinite period from 1 June 2026`

`an order suspending the charity itself` MEANS `Order proposed under Article 14(3)` WITH
    kind IS `an order suspending or removing a governor or another person concerned in the management`
    `directed at` IS `the charity`
    forbids IS NOTHING
    `it appears to the court that the person at whom the order is directed has engaged in misconduct or is responsible for it` IS FALSE
    period IS `an indefinite period from 1 June 2026`

`a hold on property directed at the bank holding the charity's funds` MEANS `Order proposed under Article 14(3)` WITH
    kind IS `an order requiring a holder of property not to part with it without the court's consent`
    `directed at` IS `a person who holds property on behalf of the charity`
    forbids IS NOTHING
    `it appears to the court that the person at whom the order is directed has engaged in misconduct or is responsible for it` IS FALSE
    period IS `an indefinite period from 1 June 2026`

`a hold on property directed at the bank holding a governor's funds` MEANS `Order proposed under Article 14(3)` WITH
    kind IS `an order requiring a holder of property not to part with it without the court's consent`
    `directed at` IS `a person who holds property on behalf of a governor of the charity`
    forbids IS NOTHING
    `it appears to the court that the person at whom the order is directed has engaged in misconduct or is responsible for it` IS FALSE
    period IS `an indefinite period from 1 June 2026`

`a hold on property directed at the charity itself` MEANS `Order proposed under Article 14(3)` WITH
    kind IS `an order requiring a holder of property not to part with it without the court's consent`
    `directed at` IS `the charity`
    forbids IS NOTHING
    `it appears to the court that the person at whom the order is directed has engaged in misconduct or is responsible for it` IS FALSE
    period IS `an indefinite period from 1 June 2026`

`an order restricting payments` MEANS `Order proposed under Article 14(3)` WITH
    kind IS `an order restricting transactions or payments without the court's consent`
    `directed at` IS `no person in particular`
    forbids IS NOTHING
    `it appears to the court that the person at whom the order is directed has engaged in misconduct or is responsible for it` IS FALSE
    period IS `the period of a hold on payments, from 1 June 2026 for 30 days`

`an order putting the administration under supervision` MEANS `Order proposed under Article 14(3)` WITH
    kind IS `an order subjecting the administration to supervision, restraint or conditions`
    `directed at` IS `no person in particular`
    forbids IS NOTHING
    `it appears to the court that the person at whom the order is directed has engaged in misconduct or is responsible for it` IS FALSE
    period IS `the period of a hold on payments, from 1 June 2026 for 30 days`

`an order to remedy, directed at a governor who appears to have engaged in misconduct` MEANS `Order proposed under Article 14(3)` WITH
    kind IS `an order requiring a person to take steps to remedy the effects of misconduct`
    `directed at` IS `a governor of the charity`
    forbids IS NOTHING
    `it appears to the court that the person at whom the order is directed has engaged in misconduct or is responsible for it` IS TRUE
    period IS `an indefinite period from 1 June 2026`

`an order to remedy, directed at a governor against whom nothing appears` MEANS `Order proposed under Article 14(3)` WITH
    kind IS `an order requiring a person to take steps to remedy the effects of misconduct`
    `directed at` IS `a governor of the charity`
    forbids IS NOTHING
    `it appears to the court that the person at whom the order is directed has engaged in misconduct or is responsible for it` IS FALSE
    period IS `an indefinite period from 1 June 2026`

`an order to remedy, directed at another person who appears responsible` MEANS `Order proposed under Article 14(3)` WITH
    kind IS `an order requiring a person to take steps to remedy the effects of misconduct`
    `directed at` IS `another person who appears to be responsible for misconduct`
    forbids IS NOTHING
    `it appears to the court that the person at whom the order is directed has engaged in misconduct or is responsible for it` IS TRUE
    period IS `an indefinite period from 1 June 2026`

`an order to remedy, directed at a stranger` MEANS `Order proposed under Article 14(3)` WITH
    kind IS `an order requiring a person to take steps to remedy the effects of misconduct`
    `directed at` IS `any other person`
    forbids IS NOTHING
    `it appears to the court that the person at whom the order is directed has engaged in misconduct or is responsible for it` IS TRUE
    period IS `an indefinite period from 1 June 2026`

`an order making ancillary provision` MEANS `Order proposed under Article 14(3)` WITH
    kind IS `an order making ancillary provision`
    `directed at` IS `no person in particular`
    forbids IS NOTHING
    `it appears to the court that the person at whom the order is directed has engaged in misconduct or is responsible for it` IS FALSE
    period IS `an indefinite period from 1 June 2026`

-- (a): directed at the charity or a governor, and saying what it forbids ((i), (ii) or (iii)).
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` `a prohibition on holding out as a charity, directed at the charity`
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` `a prohibition on soliciting donations, directed at a governor`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` `a prohibition that says nothing of what it forbids`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` `a prohibition directed at a person holding property for the charity`
-- (b), (c), (f), (g), (i): no person is named.
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` `an order appointing a manager`
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` `an order appointing a governor`
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` `an order restricting payments`
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` `an order putting the administration under supervision`
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` `an order making ancillary provision`
-- (d): a governor, or any other person concerned in the management or control of the charity; not the charity.
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` `an order suspending a governor`
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` `an order removing the finance manager`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` `an order suspending the charity itself`
-- (e): a person who holds property on behalf of the charity or of a governor.
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` `a hold on property directed at the bank holding the charity's funds`
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` `a hold on property directed at the bank holding a governor's funds`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` `a hold on property directed at the charity itself`
-- (h): a governor who appears to the court to have engaged in misconduct, or any other person who appears to be responsible for it.
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` `an order to remedy, directed at a governor who appears to have engaged in misconduct`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` `an order to remedy, directed at a governor against whom nothing appears`
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` `an order to remedy, directed at another person who appears responsible`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` `an order to remedy, directed at a stranger`

-- The court's permission to make an order of a listed kind: only where the powers of 14(1) are exercisable.
-- Arguments: the interpretation; registered charity; who applied; misconduct within Article 2(10); what appears; the order.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 14(3) the court may make the order` `the favoured reading` TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` TRUE `misconduct in the administration of the charity` `an order appointing a manager` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `make an order of a kind listed in Article 14(3)` `an order appointing a person to manage the affairs of the charity in place of its governors` AT 4

-- EXPECT: STANDING MAY
#TRACE `Art 14(3) the court may make the order` `the favoured reading` TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` TRUE `misconduct in the administration of the charity` `an order appointing a manager` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- A kind the paragraph does not allow as proposed (suspending the charity itself): no permission under (3).
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 14(3) the court may make the order` `the favoured reading` TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` TRUE `misconduct in the administration of the charity` `an order suspending the charity itself` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- The powers of 14(1) are not exercisable (an application by the registered charity): no order under (3).
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 14(3) the court may make the order` `the favoured reading` TRUE `an application by the registered charity` TRUE `misconduct in the administration of the charity` `an order appointing a manager` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- The period of an order.  Fork F5.9.  Reading A (taken): a period of 30 days from 1 June 2026 runs from 1 June to 30 June inclusive.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(3) the order is in operation on the day` `the favoured reading` `the period of a hold on payments, from 1 June 2026 for 30 days` (YMD 2026 5 31)
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is in operation on the day` `the favoured reading` `the period of a hold on payments, from 1 June 2026 for 30 days` (YMD 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is in operation on the day` `the favoured reading` `the period of a hold on payments, from 1 June 2026 for 30 days` (YMD 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(3) the order is in operation on the day` `the favoured reading` `the period of a hold on payments, from 1 June 2026 for 30 days` (YMD 2026 7 1)
-- Reading B: the period starts on the day after the first day named, so it runs from 2 June to 1 July.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(3) the order is in operation on the day` `the interpretation with the court period starting the day after` `the period of a hold on payments, from 1 June 2026 for 30 days` (YMD 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is in operation on the day` `the interpretation with the court period starting the day after` `the period of a hold on payments, from 1 June 2026 for 30 days` (YMD 2026 6 2)
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is in operation on the day` `the interpretation with the court period starting the day after` `the period of a hold on payments, from 1 June 2026 for 30 days` (YMD 2026 7 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(3) the order is in operation on the day` `the interpretation with the court period starting the day after` `the period of a hold on payments, from 1 June 2026 for 30 days` (YMD 2026 7 2)
-- An indefinite period runs on from the first day named.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(3) the order is in operation on the day` `the favoured reading` `an indefinite period from 1 June 2026` (YMD 2026 5 31)
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is in operation on the day` `the favoured reading` `an indefinite period from 1 June 2026` (YMD 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is in operation on the day` `the favoured reading` `an indefinite period from 1 June 2026` (YMD 2040 1 1)
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the first day of the period` `the favoured reading` (YMD 2026 6 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 1
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the first day of the period` `the interpretation with the court period starting the day after` (YMD 2026 6 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 2

§§ `Article 14(4): amending or revoking an order`

-- src:424 | (4) The court may, on the application of the Commissioner, the Attorney General, the registered charity or any person to whom the order was directed, amend or revoke any order made under this Article.
-- The four who may apply, and a fifth who may not.
#ASSERT `Art 14(4) the application is by one of the four` `an application by the Commissioner`
#ASSERT `Art 14(4) the application is by one of the four` `an application by the Attorney General`
#ASSERT `Art 14(4) the application is by one of the four` `an application by the registered charity`
#ASSERT `Art 14(4) the application is by one of the four` `an application by a person to whom the order was directed`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(4) the application is by one of the four` `an application by any other person`

-- Arguments: registered charity; someone is acting as the Commissioner; who applied; the order was made under Article 14.
-- The charity applies and the court amends.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 14(4) the court may amend or revoke an order` TRUE TRUE `an application by the registered charity` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `apply to the court` `an application by the registered charity` AT 3
    PARTY `the court` DOES `amend or revoke an order made under Article 14` AT 9

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 14(4) the court may amend or revoke an order` TRUE TRUE `an application by a person to whom the order was directed` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `any person` DOES `apply to the court` `an application by a person to whom the order was directed` AT 3
    PARTY `the court` DOES `amend or revoke an order made under Article 14` AT 9

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 14(4) the court may amend or revoke an order` TRUE TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `apply to the court` `an application by the Commissioner` AT 3
    PARTY `the court` DOES `amend or revoke an order made under Article 14` AT 9

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 14(4) the court may amend or revoke an order` TRUE TRUE `an application by the Attorney General` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Attorney General` DOES `apply to the court` `an application by the Attorney General` AT 3
    PARTY `the court` DOES `amend or revoke an order made under Article 14` AT 9

-- The application is made; the court has not yet acted: its permission is open.  No ground is needed (the grounds of 14(1) are not asked).
-- EXPECT: STANDING MAY
#TRACE `Art 14(4) the court may amend or revoke an order` TRUE TRUE `an application by the registered charity` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `apply to the court` `an application by the registered charity` AT 3

-- An application by anyone else opens no power.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 14(4) the court may amend or revoke an order` TRUE TRUE `an application by any other person` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- An order that was not made under Article 14 is not one this paragraph reaches.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 14(4) the court may amend or revoke an order` TRUE TRUE `an application by the registered charity` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- Nobody is acting as the Commissioner: the Commissioner has no application to make.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 14(4) the court may amend or revoke an order` TRUE FALSE `an application by the Commissioner` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

§§ `Article 14(5) and (6): the powers are additional, apply despite the constitution, and leave the Commissioner's powers alone`

-- src:425 | (5) The powers of the court under this Article apply –
-- src:426 | (a) in addition to and not in derogation from any powers of the court under any other enactment or under customary law; and
-- src:427 | (b) despite anything in the constitution of the charity.
-- (a): in addition to, and not in derogation from, the court's powers elsewhere.
#ASSERT `Art 14(5)(a) the court may act under Article 14 or under another power` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 14(5)(a) the court may act under Article 14 or under another power` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 14(5)(a) the court may act under Article 14 or under another power` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(5)(a) the court may act under Article 14 or under another power` FALSE FALSE
-- (b): a provision of the constitution forbidding the order changes nothing.
#ASSERT `Art 14(5)(b) the powers of the court under Article 14 are exercisable despite the constitution` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 14(5)(b) the powers of the court under Article 14 are exercisable despite the constitution` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(5)(b) the powers of the court under Article 14 are exercisable despite the constitution` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(5)(b) the powers of the court under Article 14 are exercisable despite the constitution` FALSE FALSE
-- Together: Article 14 powers exercisable, the constitution forbids: the court may still act; Article 14 powers not exercisable, but another power exists: it may act; neither: it may not.
#ASSERT `Art 14(5) the powers apply in addition to other powers and despite the constitution` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 14(5) the powers apply in addition to other powers and despite the constitution` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(5) the powers apply in addition to other powers and despite the constitution` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(5) the powers apply in addition to other powers and despite the constitution` FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- src:428 | (6) The powers of the court under this Article are without prejudice to any power of the Commissioner to take any action under this Law in respect of any misconduct.
-- 14(6): the Commissioner's own power is the same whether or not the court has acted.
#ASSERT `Art 14(6) the Commissioner's own power is unaffected by the powers of the court` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 14(6) the Commissioner's own power is unaffected by the powers of the court` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(6) the Commissioner's own power is unaffected by the powers of the court` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(6) the Commissioner's own power is unaffected by the powers of the court` FALSE FALSE
